<title>SINGAPORE: India sells 25,000/t Oct naphtha to Swiss trader.</title>
<headline>India sells 25,000/t Oct naphtha to Swiss trader.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold by tender 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) to a Swiss trader at $28.54 per tonne below spot Mediterrenean quotes on a free-on-board basis (fob), traders said Monday.</p>
<p>The naphtha is for lifting from Vizag between October 13-15. The tender closed on October 2 and offers were valid until October 4.</p>
<p>The last sell tender awarded ex-Vizag was to trader Vitol at $32.39 below Mediterranean quotes for lifting September 8-10.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
